      "hints": [
        "Apply the generalized binomial expansion with index $2/3$ and term $3x$.",
        "Write the coefficients successively as $n$, $n(n-1)/2!$, and $n(n-1)(n-2)/3!$ before multiplying by $(3x)^r$.",
        "Simplify each coefficient and stop after the $x^3$ term."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the general binomial series expansion $(1 + u)^n = 1 + nu + \\dfrac{n(n - 1)}{2!}u^2 + \\dfrac{n(n - 1)(n - 2)}{3!}u^3 + \\dots$ with $u = 3x$ and $n = \\dfrac{2}{3}$:",
        "Calculate the first term:\n$$1$$",
        "Calculate the linear term in $x$:\n$$n(3x) = \\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)(3x) = 2x$$",
        "Calculate the quadratic term in $x^2$:\n$$\\dfrac{\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\frac{2}{3} - 1\\right)}{2!}(3x)^2 = \\dfrac{\\frac{2}{3}\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}{2}(9x^2) = \\dfrac{-\\frac{2}{9}}{2}(9x^2) = -\\dfrac{1}{9}(9x^2) = -x^2$$",
        "Calculate the cubic term in $x^3$:\n$$\\dfrac{\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\frac{2}{3} - 1\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{3} - 2\\right)}{3!}(3x)^3 = \\dfrac{\\frac{2}{3}\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{4}{3}\\right)}{6}(27x^3) = \\dfrac{\\frac{8}{27}}{6}(27x^3) = \\dfrac{8}{6}x^3 = \\dfrac{4}{3}x^3$$",
        "Combine all terms to state the expansion up to $x^3$:\n$$(1 + 3x)^{\\frac{2}{3}} = 1 + 2x - x^2 + \\dfrac{4}{3}x^3 + \\dots$$"
      ],
